From e5fe445b4019d8a5c94dd5f664ad80c0f293411a Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Valery Petrov <valerypetrov@icloud.com>
Date: Sun, 6 Sep 2026 04:09:45 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Acknowledge a distributed remote write only once every shard
 target is still the table checked

The shard-target check ran before the INSERT and nothing ran after it: a
same-schema table swapped in under a shard-local name between the two took
the batch, and the write was acknowledged into it. The write now records
what every replica holds (engine, `time_series` type, table UUID) in the
check and asks again after the delivery; any difference, or a replica that
cannot be asked again, leaves the write unacknowledged with
UNKNOWN_STATUS_OF_INSERT (a retryable 500), so Prometheus resends the batch
and the next check refuses it. A table swapped in and back within one
request is not seen. A DDL guard on a shard that is this server was tried
and dropped: it serializes every concurrent write on that node.

A pausable failpoint between the check and the INSERT lets the tests swap a
target meanwhile, both over the connection and in-process.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5.1 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_016i1XnLC3KypZdaYYsfzqub
